{%- comment -%}
  won-fx — resolves the theme-wide CTA effect settings into the class list every
  won button wears. ONE place, so a new section cannot ship a button that quietly
  sits outside the effect layer (which is exactly how the card quick-add ended up
  with no hover state at all while `.won-btn` had one).

  Render it INSIDE the class attribute of any interactive won CTA:

    <a class="won-btn won-btn--primary {% render 'won-fx' %}" href="…">…</a>

  Deliberately NOT on non-actions: a sold-out label must not animate as if it
  could be clicked.

  The effects themselves live in assets/won-tokens.css (§ CTA effect layer) and
  are driven purely by these classes — no inline style, so the markup stays
  cacheable and a store's whole button signature is four selects in the theme
  editor (themes/build/won-effect-settings.json).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign fx_hover = settings.won_btn_hover | default: 'lift'
  assign fx_sheen = settings.won_btn_sheen | default: 'hover'
  assign fx_press = settings.won_btn_press | default: 'sink'
  assign fx_speed = settings.won_fx_speed | default: 'normal'
  echo 'won-fx won-fx--hover-'
  echo fx_hover
  echo ' won-fx--sheen-'
  echo fx_sheen
  echo ' won-fx--press-'
  echo fx_press
  echo ' won-fx--speed-'
  echo fx_speed
-%}
